Dan "'''apEX'''" Madesclaire {{born}} is a [[:Category:France|French]] professional ''[[Counter-Strike 2]]'' player who plays for [[Team Vitality]] as the [[:Category:In-game leaders|in-game leader]] and an [[:Category:Entry fraggers|entry fragger]] and a former ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' and ''[[Counter-Strike: Source]]'' player. An entry fragger in the earlier days of ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive|Global Offensive]]'', known for his aggression; he transitioned to the [[:Category:In-game leaders|IGL]] role in March 2020 after [[ALEX_(British_player)|ALEX]]'s departure from [[Team Vitality]].

apEX is among the most decorated players in ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive|Global Offensive]]'' and ''[[Counter-Strike 2]]'' history, having won over 35 [[S-Tier Tournaments|S-Tier]] tournaments across his career. Among these accomplishments include four [[Majors]] and two [[ESL/Grand Slam|ESL Grand Slam]] trophies.

